I've been casually playing NetHack (currently, MacOS Qt tileset) on
and off for about ten years, but I've never ascended. My latest
attempt was by far my best, but there are some details regarding the
death which I can't make sense of.

I was a human valkyrie with a lot of things going for me, although my
armor still wasn't fire/rust-proof and my Excalibur had been sunk to
+0 by a series of disenchanters. I had finished my Quest and was
tooling around Gehennom looking for wishes, markers, or a way to make
holy water, but was otherwise ready for Rodney. I had two amulets of
life saving, one of which I was wearing. I was also wearing blessed
gauntlets of power. On level 47 of the mazes, things got a little
weird.

I encountered a dog and killed it in one hit. No big deal.

> But wait... The dog's medallion begins to glow!
> The dog looks much better.
> The dog's medallion crumbles to dust!

Instead of a dog reappearing, I see a trapper instead. Ok, I assume
this is a chameleon. Attack it again, and it's dead for good.

Not long after, I encounter a cockatrice. I killed it and wielded the
corpse. Another cockatrice appears, I hit it twice before realizing
attacking a cockatrice with another cockatrice is entirely stupid. I
switch weapons, but before I can get a hit in, I read:

> The cockatrice touches you
> You hear the cockatrice's hissing!
> You are slowing down.

Well, balls. I'm in Gehonnom, so I can't pray. It's too late to zap it
with a wand of cancellation. But at least I have an amulet of life
saving on, so I'll just let this happen and move on.

> Your limbs are stiffening.

Yeah yeah, just get it over with.

> You have turned to stone.
> Do you want your possessions identified?

What?!

As it turns out, I was no longer wearing an amulet of life saving
(although I still had the other in my bag). On my attributes, it said
I had been killed two times.

The thing is, I have no recollection of dying the first time. I'll
grant it's possible it happened and I didn't notice, but that isn't
the sort of thing I would forget.

So, what the hell happened?


